			<div class="content" id="post-content-3615541">
									

<p>Upvoted with reservations. I love Sumer and Ara Orun, but the former felt underused. A lot of the same alt dimension skip cliches we usually see (like the camera mysteriously working again long after it originally failed) were present but packaged in Sumerian paint. It would have been more interesting if it were more distinctly Sumerian.</p>
<p>The dialogue is a bit hamfisted. Asking if he’s going to die conveys his attitude quite well, going on to describe the place in melodramatic terms just feels blunt in a bad way. We get it, the place is spooky.</p>
<p>The piece could def be something great, but it’s not quite there atm.</p>

